OL,3,GNEWSAHundreds protest plan for
OL,4,Ayear-round dog beach ban
OL,5,
OL,6,FHundreds of dogs and their owners
OL,7,Fdescended on a beach to protest against
OL,8,Fa planned year-round ban.
OL,10,FIf approved, dogs would be banned from
OL,11,Fthe Cayley Promenade section of the
OL,12,Fbeach in Rhos-on-Sea, Conwy, which is
OL,13,Fbetween already dog-free areas at the
OL,14,Fharbour and Porth Eirias.
OL,16,FConwy councillor Jo Nuttall, also a
OL,17,FRhos-on-Sea town councillor, said
OL,18,Fcreating another no-go area would
OL,19,Fdisproportionately penalise owners.
OL,23,APub: 23-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,439,430,260,140,0,100
